Package: cloud-apt-info
Version: 0.1.0-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: cloud-apt example <noreply@example.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: python3
Description: cloud-apt companion example (Python)
 A pure-Python example package used to verify that cloud-apt
 migration handles multiple packages without mixing their pool
 paths. Distinct from cloud-apt-hello in three ways:
 .
   - Python source instead of C (no compile step)
   - Depends on python3 instead of libc6
   - Drops a config file under /etc/cloud-apt so postinst must
     create a directory before writing the file
 .
 Exposes /usr/bin/cloud-apt-info and /usr/local/bin/cloud-apt-info
 (via symlink created in postinst). Supports --version, --repo,
 --config, and --health flags.
